{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define mod 1000000007\n#define N 33\n#define int long long\nint bin[N*2],n,m;\nstruct matrix{ \n    int mat[N][N];\n    inline matrix operator * (const matrix &a) const {\n        matrix res;\n        memset(res.mat,0,sizeof(res.mat));\n        for (int i=0;i<=m;++i){\n            for (int j=0;j<=m;++j){\n                for (int k=0;k<=m;++k){\n                    res.mat[i][j]=(res.mat[i][j]+mat[i][k]*a.mat[k][j])%mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n}ans,P[N*2][N],S[N*2][N],A[N*2][N];\nint read(){\n    int x=0,f=1;\n    char ch=getchar();\n    while (ch<'0' || ch>'9'){\n        if (ch=='-') f=-1;\n        ch=getchar();\n    }\n    while (ch>='0' && ch<='9'){\n        x=x*10+ch-'0';ch=getchar();\n    }\n    return x*f;\n}\nsigned main(){\n    n=read(),m=read();\n    int n2=n,len=-1;\n    while (n2){ \n        len++;bin[len]=n2%m;n2=n2/m;\n    }\n    len++;\n    for (int i=0;i<=m;++i) ans.mat[0][i]=1; \n    for (int i=0;i<len;++i){\n        for (int j=0;j<=m;++j) A[i][0].mat[j][j]=1;\n        if (!i){ \n            for (int j=0;j<m;++j){\n                A[i][j].mat[m][m]=1;\n                for (int k=0;k<m;++k){\n                    if (k!=j){\n                        A[i][j].mat[k][k]=1;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    for (int l=0;l<=m;++l) A[i][j].mat[k][l]=1;\n                }\n            }\n        }else{\n            for (int j=0;j<m;++j){\n                if (!j) A[i][j]=S[i-1][0]; \n                else A[i][j]=S[i-1][j]*P[i-1][j-1];\n            }\n        }\n        P[i][0]=A[i][0];\n        for (int j=1;j<m;++j) P[i][j]=P[i][j-1]*A[i][j];\n        S[i][m-1]=A[i][m-1];\n        for (int j=m-2;j>=0;--j) S[i][j]=A[i][j]*S[i][j+1];\n    }\n    int j=0;\n    for (int i=len-1;i>=0;--i){\n        while (bin[i] --> 0){\n            ans=ans*A[i][j];j++;if (j==m) j=0;\n        }\n    }\n    cout<<ans.mat[0][m]<<endl;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, m):\n    \"\"\"Multiply two (m+1)x(m+1) matrices modulo MOD.\"\"\"\n    size = m + 1\n    C = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        for k in range(size):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(size):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef mat_identity(m):\n    size = m + 1\n    I = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        I[i][i] = 1\n    return I\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n\n    # Compute base-m digits of n (least significant first)\n    digits = []\n    n2 = n\n    while n2:\n        digits.append(n2 % m)\n        n2 //= m\n    if not digits:\n        digits = [0]\n    L = len(digits)  # number of digits\n\n    # Initialize ans as a matrix with first row all 1, rest 0\n    size = m + 1\n    ans = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for j in range(size):\n        ans[0][j] = 1\n\n    # Prepare storage for A, P, S matrices\n    A = [[None] * m for _ in range(L)]\n    P = [[None] * m for _ in range(L)]\n    S = [[None] * m for _ in range(L)]\n\n    for i in range(L):\n        if i == 0:\n            # i = 0: special construction\n            for j in range(m):\n                mat = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n                # Set last row (index m) to identity (only diagonal)\n                mat[m][m] = 1\n                for k in range(m):\n                    if k != j:\n                        mat[k][k] = 1\n                    else:\n                        # row j: all ones\n                        for l in range(size):\n                            mat[k][l] = 1\n                A[i][j] = mat\n        else:\n            # i > 0: use S[i-1] and P[i-1]\n            A[i][0] = S[i-1][0]\n            for j in range(1, m):\n                A[i][j] = mat_mul(S[i-1][j], P[i-1][j-1], m)\n\n        # Compute prefix products P[i][j]\n        P[i][0] = A[i][0]\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            P[i][j] = mat_mul(P[i][j-1], A[i][j], m)\n\n        # Compute suffix products S[i][j]\n        S[i][m-1] = A[i][m-1]\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            S[i][j] = mat_mul(A[i][j], S[i][j+1], m)\n\n    # Main loop over digits from most significant to least\n    j = 0\n    for i in range(L-1, -1, -1):\n        d = digits[i]\n        for _ in range(d):\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, A[i][j], m)\n            j = (j + 1) % m\n\n    # Output the required element\n    print(ans[0][m] % MOD)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00035768310772255063, -0.015334565192461014, 0.0, -0.0015049570938572288, -0.08372809737920761, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 